1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
ReCo-Splat reconstructs compact and expressive three-dimensional Gaussian maps from sparse, unposed images in a single forward pass.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:14,000
As more views are added, rendering quality saturates, while the number of predicted Gaussians continues to grow.

3
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:20,000
Red regions identify surfaces repeatedly explained by multiple views, which are the targets of inter-view compaction.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
The model fuses geometry and appearance features, allocates primitives according to local complexity, and compresses cross-view redundancy through opacity competition.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,000
A compact representation still preserves stable textures, thin structures, and high-frequency details in novel views.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
Depth reconstruction retains sharper boundaries and produces more continuous local surfaces across challenging scenes.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:48,000
The auditorium sequence pairs the rendered view with predicted depth.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:52,000
The Family scene preserves the sculpture and its surrounding context.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:56,000
This outdoor sequence demonstrates stability in a cluttered real environment.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:00,000
A second real sequence covers a larger indoor structure.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Along the same camera trajectory, DA3 and WorldMirror produce denser or less balanced distributions, while ReCo-Splat remains compact and follows the scene surfaces.

12
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:24,000
Comparing the RGB reference, DA3, WorldMirror, and our result shows that the Gaussian budget is concentrated where appearance and geometry require more detail.

13
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:27,500
The first frame reveals the Gaussian structure around the sculpture.

14
00:01:27,500 --> 00:01:31,000
The second frame preserves detailed indoor coverage.

15
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,500
The third frame contains complex textures and boundaries.

16
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:38,000
The fourth frame demonstrates compact coverage in a larger room.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,000
At two hundred fifty-five K pixels, ReCo-Splat uses about zero point eight million Gaussians and supports up to seventy input images.

18
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Ablations confirm that intra-view allocation and inter-view compaction jointly reduce active Gaussians while preserving rendering quality.

19
00:01:52,000 --> 00:02:00,000
ReCo-Splat delivers strong capacity, stable geometry, and high-quality novel-view synthesis with significantly fewer Gaussian primitives.
